			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic superhero film in the visual aesthetic of the Fox X-Men movies, with realistic lighting, cool metallic colors, intense kinetic camerawork, strong depth parallax, and physically detailed high-speed effects. The entire sequence unfolds at full real-time speed with continuous forward motion. An extreme-low-angle close-up begins only twenty centimeters above the wet asphalt, framing the rapidly striking shoes of the same Quicksilver throughout the video. He is a lean young man with wind-swept silver-white hair, silver protective goggles, a metallic silver leather jacket, a dark graphic shirt, black trousers, and running shoes. His first foot slams into a puddle and launches a long sheet of water backward. He immediately explodes into a sprint, each powerful stride covering several meters. The camera moves backward directly in front of him in a Tracking Shot with large amplitude at fast speed, rapidly Pulling Out from his shoes to reveal his full running body. Lane markings flash beneath him in rapid succession, nearby streetlights flicker across his face like a strobe, and the road surface becomes a continuous stream beneath his feet. His torso and face remain sharply readable while his arms and legs carry controlled directional motion blur.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.200, the camera cuts to a low side-on Tracking Shot racing parallel with Quicksilver at fast speed. He accelerates hard along a Manhattan avenue and overtakes multiple moving taxis within a few strides. Every step throws a narrow explosion of water and compressed air behind him. Lamp posts, traffic signs, parked cars, bridge supports, and foreground columns sweep across the lens as rapid full-frame wipes, producing powerful foreground parallax. The camera shakes slightly under the air pressure while struggling to keep him centered. Quicksilver lowers his shoulders, increases his stride length, and runs even faster; the windows, streetlights, and building façades stretch into long horizontal bands while he remains a single coherent silver-clad figure. A tightly compressed silver-blue pressure wake forms behind his body as loose paper and road mist are violently pulled into his path.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.000, the camera cuts to a long-lens Static Shot looking straight down six city blocks. Quicksilver first appears as a tiny silver figure at the distant intersection. He crosses the entire distance in less than one second, growing from a speck to a full-frame figure with extreme perspective expansion. His footsteps merge into one continuous thunderous vibration. He passes within centimeters of the lens as a concentrated silver streak. The camera immediately Pans Right with large amplitude at fast speed to chase him, but he is already hundreds of meters farther down the avenue. A delayed pressure wave slams into the camera, violently spraying rainwater across the lens, rocking nearby vehicles, bending street signs, and blasting newspapers high into the air.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:06.600, the camera cuts to an extreme-high-angle aerial Tracking Shot moving above Quicksilver at fast speed. He covers an entire city block every few strides, sharply changes direction around moving traffic, crosses three intersections before the lights can visibly change, and accelerates through a narrow gap between two buses. Circular shock rings expand through puddles several meters behind each footfall. The camera Pedestals Down with large amplitude at fast speed and transitions into a close rear chase shot directly behind him. Quicksilver glances over his shoulder for a fraction of a second, gives a confident smirk, then leans forward and launches into one final acceleration. The camera races after him but rapidly loses distance. He becomes a narrow silver point, crosses several more blocks, and vanishes around a distant corner before the camera reaches the next intersection. A visible compression wave continues racing down the avenue after him, sweeping water, fog, and loose debris outward in a widening corridor.\n\noverall_soundscape: Quicksilver’s individual footsteps accelerate until they merge into a continuous mechanical thunder beneath the roar of displaced air. Tires, engines, rain, and city noise produce rapidly shifting Doppler tones as he overtakes them. Each acceleration creates sharp pressure cracks, explosive sprays of water, rattling windows, and a final delayed sonic boom that rolls between the buildings after he has disappeared.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A relentless 180-BPM rhythm driven by rapid drum-kit strikes, distorted electric-bass pulses, sixteenth-note rhythm guitar, and short analog-synth bursts. The percussion adds faster subdivisions with every acceleration, then stops for a fraction of a second immediately before the final sonic boom.",
				1344,
				768,
				73
			],
